.Dd January 31, 2026
.Dt CMDLINE 9
.Os Substrate
.Sh NAME
.Nm cmdline
.Nd kernel command line parameters
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The Substrate kernel accepts various command line parameters at boot time to configure system behavior, hardware drivers, and debugging options.
.Sh PARAMETERS
.Bl -tag -width "syscall_trace"
.It Sy root=device
Specifies the device to mount as the root filesystem.
Example:
.Li root=/dev/hda1
.It Sy rootfstype=type
Specifies the filesystem type of the root device. Default is
.Li ext2 .
.It Sy init=path
Specifies the path to the init process binary.
Default search order:
.Li /sbin/init ,
.Li /etc/init ,
.Li /bin/init ,
.Li /bin/sh .
.It Sy video=mode
Configures the video driver or mode.
Supported values:
.Bl -tag -width "hercules" -compact
.It Li off , none
Disable framebuffer/video driver.
.It Li ask
Determine video mode via interactive menu (planned).
.It Li cfa , cga
Force CGA text mode (0xB8000).
.It Li ega
Force EGA text mode (0xB8000).
.It Li hercules , mono
Force MDA/Hercules monochrome text mode (0xB0000).
.El
.It Sy serial_debug
Enables kernel logging output to the serial port (COM1).
.It Sy syscall_trace , syscall_log
Enables logging of all system calls to the console/serial port.
.It Sy procmem
If the init process (PID 1) crashes, dump its memory mappings to the debug output.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr boot 8 ,
.Xr init 8
.Sh AUTHORS
.An The Substrate Project
